            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0487" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/1092: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-27T18:00:00+00:00">November 27,
                            1939—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 27—5:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2837. The British Ambassador said to me today that Sir Percy Loraine, British
                    Ambassador in Rome, had passed through Paris yesterday and had said to him that
                    he was absolutely certain that Mussolini himself had turned away from Germany
                    and was much more <pb facs="0488" n="476" xml:id="pg476"/> favorable to France
                    and England than he had been in the past. He added that Loraine was confident
                    that this evolution would continue provided the French and British should have
                    sufficient discretion not to talk about it.</p>
                <p>Sir Ronald Campbell also said to me that his Government did not believe that
                    there was any chance that the Japanese and Soviet Governments would reach
                    agreement for a division of China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
